UPDATE companies SET description='Electrical Equipment LLC has operated from Idaho Falls, Idaho since 1962. The company was founded by Brook Jensen, a licensed Master Electrician who continues to lead the business as owner and president. Jensen brought over 30 years of hands-on electrical experience across residential, commercial, and industrial sectors when he established the firm.

The contractor provides full-spectrum electrical services through six primary divisions: residential, commercial, industrial, agricultural, generators & emergency power, and government & institutional. Its 8 licensed electricians handle panel upgrades, EV charger installations, LED lighting retrofits, three-phase power distribution, motor controls and VFDs, motor control centers, switchgear maintenance, conduit systems, irrigation pump wiring, grain bin and elevator systems, barn and outbuilding wiring, generator connections, automatic and manual transfer switches, UPS coordination, and standby power testing. The team commits to a 2-hour emergency response for critical outages and serves a 200-mile radius across Eastern Idaho.

Customers include homeowners, business and property managers, manufacturing and processing plants, farms, dairies, and government-adjacent facilities such as the BEA and INL area. The company is SAM.gov registered (UEI: DZU2WXSS6K6) and maintains OSHA and NFPA 70E compliance with a written lockout/tagout safety program.

Electrical Equipment LLC emphasizes integrity, safety, and documentation. Every job includes before-and-after photos, test readings, and written completion reports. The firm carries a Master Electrician license, $1 million general liability insurance, workers compensation, and $1 million bonding. Jobs are managed through professional software for real-time scheduling, digital invoicing, and complete job history.', certifications=ARRAY['OSHA 10','OSHA 30','NFPA 70E','SAM.gov registered (UEI: DZU2WXSS6K6)','Idaho Master Electrician License #052024','Idaho Electrical Contractor License #056784','$1M General Liability Insurance','$1M Bonding','Workers Compensation Insurance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential electrical services (panel upgrades, new circuits, GFCI/AFCI protection, EV charger installation, home safety inspections, ceiling fans & lighting)", "Commercial electrical maintenance (preventive maintenance programs, LED lighting retrofits, lighting controls & sensors, tenant improvement wiring, emergency & exit lighting, code compliance upgrades)", "Industrial electrical systems (three-phase power distribution, motor controls & VFDs, motor control centers (MCCs), switchgear & panel maintenance, conduit systems, planned outage coordination)", "Agricultural electrical systems (irrigation pump wiring, grain bin & elevator systems, barn & outbuilding wiring, livestock facility power, weatherproof installations, load management systems)", "Generator & emergency power (generator connections & hookup, automatic transfer switches, manual transfer switches, UPS system coordination, emergency lighting systems, standby power testing)", "Government & institutional electrical services (SAM.gov registered, OSHA & NFPA 70E compliant, written LOTO safety program, full documentation & reporting, work authorization compliance)"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Government", "Institutional"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "2-hour emergency response for critical outages", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Master Electrician on every job", "Safety program with LOTO policy, NFPA 70E compliance, arc flash PPE, and mandatory test-before-touch", "Documented work including before/after photos, test readings, and written completion reports", "2-hour emergency response for critical outages and safety hazards", "Licensed, insured, and bonded with $1M general liability and $1M bonding"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1962 -> db", "Headquarters Idaho Falls, Idaho -> db", "Owner Brook Jensen, Licensed Master Electrician -> /", "8 licensed electricians -> /", "2-hour emergency response -> /", "SAM.gov registered UEI DZU2WXSS6K6 -> /", "OSHA 10/30, NFPA 70E certified -> /", "$1M GL insurance, $1M bonding -> /", "Services: residential, commercial, industrial, agricultural, generators, government -> /", "Serves Eastern Idaho within 200-mile radius -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Licensed electrical contractors serving residential, commercial, industrial, and agricultural customers across Eastern Idaho.", "founded_year": "1962", "employee_count": "8 licensed electricians", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='electrical-equipment-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Electrical Materials Company has operated from Earlville, Illinois since its founding in 1961. The business also maintains a facility in Genoa City, Wisconsin.

The company manufactures a range of pole‑line and underground distribution hardware for electric utilities, telephone and CATV providers. Its product line includes cable enclosures, guy markers, U‑Guard™ pole risers (both steel and plastic), wildlife protectors, transformer accessories, secondary service pedestals (steel rounded, rectangular or square), RV and mobile‑home power pedestals (metered and unmetered), mounting posts, brackets, ground‑wire molding, conduit duct plugs and cable markers.

Examples from its catalog include transformer mounting cleats for utility substations, perch guards for avian protection, and ergonomic lineman tools such as blanket clamp hooks and outrigger pads.

