UPDATE companies SET description='Electronic Specialties of Connecticut, Inc. (ESC) operates from a 14,500-square-foot, climate-controlled facility in Hamden, Connecticut. The company was established in 1981 by Rich Dumont.

ESC specializes in printed circuit board assembly, handling through-hole, surface-mount, and mixed-technology builds from prototype through full production. Its high-speed Juki pick-and-place lines can place up to 60,000 components per hour, supported by a Speedline OmniMax ten-zone reflow oven, a full aqueous cleaning line, and wave soldering for both RoHS and non-RoHS runs. The shop also provides automated optical inspection (Mirtec MV-3 and MVHTL systems), manual X-ray inspection (QUADRA3 PRO), functional testing, value-added unit assembly (cable harnesses, sheet-metal and plastic integration), box-build, design and layout services, and materials management for turnkey or consigned programs.

The company serves the broader electronics industry, working with customers who need prototype quantities as well as volume production runs. It accepts both full turnkey and consigned-material arrangements and uses an MRP system to coordinate component procurement from multiple vendors.

ESC states that its mission is to exceed customer expectations for quality, service, technology, and cost while maintaining a safe, healthy workplace. It emphasizes the use of current automation and IPC-certified processes (IPC-A-610, J-STD-001) to deliver reliable assemblies and offers design input aimed at maximizing production efficiency and reducing cost.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS','IPC-A-610','J-STD-001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Through-hole assembly", "Surface-mount assembly", "Mixed-technology assembly", "Wave soldering (RoHS and non-RoHS)", "Aqueous cleaning", "Circuit modification", "Harnessing", "Packaging", "Automated optical inspection (AOI)", "X-ray inspection", "Functional testing", "Box build / unit assembly", "Prototyping", "Full production assembly", "Design services (circuit design, layout, product design)", "Materials management (turnkey and consigned)", "Value-added assembly", "Engineering services", "BGA assembly"], "industries": ["Electronics"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["JUKI RS-1R Fast Smart Modular Mounter", "QUADRA3 PRO Manual X-ray Inspection System", "MV-3 OMNI MARK-\u2161 3D AOI System", "High Speed Juki Pick and Place Line", "Juki RS-1 Fast Smart Modular Mounter", "Speedline OmniMax With Ten Zones Reflow Oven", "Full Aqueous Cleaning Line", "Mirtec MV-3 Omni Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "Mirtec MVHTL Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "Schleuniger Cut and Strip", "HEPCO Prep Machine", "Mantis and Lynx Inspection Equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Complete turnkey or consigned-material programs with MRP-driven materials management", "High-speed SMT lines placing up to 60,000 components per hour", "In-house AOI, X-ray, and functional testing", "Value-added assembly including cable, sheet-metal, and box-build", "Design and layout services to optimize manufacturability and cost"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 -> db and page ''/''", "Headquarters Hamden, CT -> db and pag