UPDATE companies SET description='Elevate Packaging is based in Chicago, Illinois. Founded in 2000 by Rich Cohen, a former corporate strategist and computer scientist at a Fortune 500 company, the business began after a 1999 sabbatical during which Cohen encountered tree-free papers made from invasive plant species. He launched the company to address the lack of viable compostable packaging alternatives.

The company develops and manufactures a full line of compostable packaging, including stand-up pouches (kraft, white, and transparent), flat pouches, cellophane bags, coffee bags, poly mailers, adhesive labels and stickers, packaging tape, and gloves. It offers custom design and full-color printing on compostable substrates, and operates a take-back program with the Compost Stewardship Institute to ensure used packaging is composted.

Elevate serves brands in natural and organic food, institutional food service, coffee and tea, cannabis, apparel, body care, e-commerce, and retail. Its solutions are used for product packaging, shipping supplies, and retail-ready packaging where compostability is required.

Cohen started the business after witnessing plastic pollution in remote wilderness areas. The company’s stated mission is to “Eliminate Plastic Waste and Create a Healthy Planet.” It differentiates itself through early commercialization of certified compostable pressure-sensitive labels (PURE Labels™), BPI-certified materials meeting ASTM D6400, and a circular-economy take-back service.', certifications=ARRAY['ASTM D6400','BPI certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom compostable packaging design", "Full-color printing on compostable materials", "Compostable label manufacturing (PURE Labels\u2122)", "Stand-up pouch manufacturing", "Flat pouch manufacturing", "Cellophane bag manufacturing", "Coffee bag manufacturing", "Poly mailer manufacturing", "Compostable adhesive sticker production", "Compostable packaging tape production", "Compostable glove production", "Compostable product take-back and composting program"], "industries": ["Natural food", "Institutional food service", "Coffee", "Tea", "Cannabis", "Apparel", "Body care", "Ecommerce", "Retail", "Organic food", "Specialty food", "Restaurant", "E-commerce shipping"], "materials": ["Natural hemp paper", "Compostable resins", "Compostable films", "Compostable adhesives", "Compostable coatings", "Kraft paper (compostable)", "Cellophane (compostable)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First and only certified compostable label in North America (PURE Labels\u2122)", "BPI-certified compostable materials meeting ASTM D6400", "Take-back program with Compost Stewardship Institute for circular composting", "Custom full-color printing on compostable substrates", "No-waste philosophy offering imperfect products at discount"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2000 by Rich Cohen -> /about", "Founder background: corporate strategy and technology innovation at Fortune 500 -> /about", "Sabbatical in 1999 led to discovery of tree-free papers from invasive plants -> /about", "Mission: ''Eliminate Plastic Waste and Create a Healthy Planet'' -> /about", "Developed compostable pressure-sensitive adhesive label by 2007 using natural hemp paper -> /about", "ASTM D6400 tests and BPI certification secured for labels -> /about", "Take-back program with Compost Stewardship Institute (CSI) -> /about", "Industries served: natural food, institutional food service, coffee, tea, cannabis, apparel, body care -> / (homepage)", "Products: stand-up pouches, flat pouches, cellophane bags, coffee bags, poly mailers, labels, stickers, tape, gloves -> / (homepage)", "Custom packaging with full-color printing -> / (homepage)", "PURE Labels\u2122 first and only certified compostable label in North America -> / (homepage) and /about", "No-waste philosophy offering imperfect products at discount -> / (homepage)", "Headquarters Chicago, Illinois -> db", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Elevate Packaging established the hard-earned reputation as the industry pioneer in commercializing novel compostable packaging solutions", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/elevatepackaging/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='elevate-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company does not publicly disclose its founding year or ownership structure.

The company produces a range of prepared foods including savory baked goods such as quiches, frittatas, and chicken pot pies, as well as dips and spreads, deli salads, and sous vide potatoes. Its capabilities span kettle cooking, baking, mixing, and filling across both refrigerated and frozen formats, with packaging options from single-serve retail to bulk foodservice sizes. Two USDA-inspected plants provide redundant capacity for national and regional distribution.

