UPDATE companies SET description='Ellerbuilt Woodworks operates from Carson City, Nevada, where founder Brandon Eller established the shop as an extension of a lifelong dedication to woodworking. Eller’s path began with childhood projects — refinishing a bench at age ten — and deepened through study of Japanese joinery traditions. The business emerged from a philosophy that craftsmanship should reflect the maker’s full attention, not merely fill a space.

The shop produces custom cabinetry and handcrafted furniture for residential interiors. Offerings span kitchen and bathroom cabinets, built-in shelving and wall units, home-office desks and partner desks, bedroom pieces such as headboards and dressers, plus kitchen islands, bar cabinets, and entertainment centers. Work combines traditional hand-tool techniques with modern machinery, and finishes include conversion varnish, catalyzed lacquer, and UV-cured coatings. Wood selection ranges from domestic hardwoods — oak, maple, cherry, walnut — to softwoods like redwood and cedar and exotic species.

Each project starts with a site visit and design consultation, followed by a detailed timeline; smaller jobs may finish in weeks, while larger commissions can require several months.

Ellerbuilt distinguishes itself through an uncompromising standard: “If something is easy to do, it’s not worth doing.” Eller visits every installation space, designs for exact fit, and insists on joinery and finishing that will endure generations. The shop’s differentiator is not speed or volume but the deliberate, risk-accepting pursuit of pieces that carry the maker’s signature.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry", "Handcrafted furniture", "Built-in cabinetry", "Custom furniture design", "Wood finishing (conversion varnish, catalyzed lacquer, UV-cured)", "Joinery", "Wood selection consultation", "Site measurement and installation"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Oak", "Maple", "Cherry", "Walnut", "Redwood", "Cedar", "Exotic woods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Smaller projects within a few weeks; larger projects several months", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Site visits and design consultation for every project", "Finishes include conversion varnish, catalyzed lacquer, and UV-cured coatings", "Blend of traditional hand-tool joinery and modern machining", "Heirloom-quality construction intended to last generations", "Wide selection of domestic and exotic wood species"], "facts_used": ["Location: Carson City, Nevada -> /", "Founder: Brandon Eller -> /", "Products: custom cabinets, handcrafted furniture, built-ins -> /", "Materials: oak, maple, cherry, walnut, redwood, cedar, exotic woods -> /", "Finishes: conversion varnish, catalyzed lacquer, UV-cured -> /", "Lead time: smaller projects weeks, larger months -> /", "Philosophy: ''If something is easy to do, it''s not worth doing'' -> /", "Process: site visits, design consultation, traditional and modern techniques -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every table, every project, every piece is the result of patience, purpose, and an artist''s relentless pursuit of excellence", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ellerbuilt-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ellis Fabrics operates in Bentonville, Arkansas, as the retail arm of Joe Ellis Upholstery. Joe Ellis began upholstering in 2002, working with independent shops in Arkansas and Louisiana. He opened Joe Ellis Upholstery in 2008, and the business grew to a larger space within five years. In 2013, Ellis and his mother, Cheryl, added a fabric store to answer frequent customer requests for fabric sources.

The business runs two workrooms staffed by nine full-time professionals plus part-time help, producing custom upholstery for residential, commercial, and specialty markets. In addition to fabrication, Ellis Fabrics stocks a range of upholstery and home décor fabrics, trims, real and faux leather, outdoor fabrics, and specialty designer materials available for special order. A design center offers in-person consultation for fabric selection and durability guidance. The shop also provides pick-up and delivery service across Northwest Arkansas, Northeast Oklahoma, and Southwest Missouri.

Customers span residential clients, hospitality venues such as restaurants, bars, museums, and hotels, medical and fitness facilities, and RV or motorhome owners. Notable accounts include the Roark Group (design/fabrication), Onyx Coffee Lab (hospitality), Laura''s Draperies & Blinds (window treatments), and various interior designers and architects across Arkansas and beyond.

