UPDATE companies SET description='ElringKlinger Manufacturing Indiana Inc. operates in Fort Wayne, Indiana, as part of the global ElringKlinger Group, a German-headquartered automotive supplier listed on the Frankfurt Stock Exchange (ISIN DE). The Indiana entity serves as a manufacturing arm for the group''s portfolio of sealing, shielding, lightweight, and electrification technologies.

The facility produces components for all vehicle drive types—combustion, hybrid, and fully electric. Core product lines include cylinder-head and specialty gaskets, thermal and acoustic shielding, formed metal parts, and assembled modules such as lithium-ion battery systems and fuel-cell stacks. The group also maintains a dedicated toolmaking technology center in Lenningen, Germany, supporting global production. Scale specifics for the Indiana site—square footage, headcount, annual volume—are not disclosed in the source material.

The company also supplies non-automotive sectors, leveraging its sealing, shielding, and lightweighting expertise for industrial applications. Concrete examples from the group''s portfolio include electric drive units, underbody systems, chassis and brake components, and aftermarket repair kits sold under the "Elring – das Original" brand.

