UPDATE companies SET description='Ernest Packaging Solutions operates a Boise-area facility in Nampa, Idaho, serving the greater Boise metro market and beyond.

The company designs, manufactures, and distributes custom packaging solutions across food, beverage, pharmaceutical, medical, cosmetics, retail, display, and industrial segments. Its offerings extend to branded packaging, sustainable and biodegradable options, temperature-controlled cold-chain packaging, and industrial-grade protective packaging. Ernest also supplies packaging equipment — including conveyor systems, case sealers, and full line integration — along with packaging and facility supplies managed through just-in-time inventory and bulk-order programs.

Customers span food and beverage producers such as Pizza Port Brewing Company and Sol-ti, pharmaceutical and medical device firms, and industrial shippers like The Rag Company and Coast Aluminum. Retail and consumer-goods clients include Carolina Coops, 7 Points, and No Toil. The company cites its client relationship managers as a differentiator, noting they proactively identify improvement areas rather than simply selling boxes.

Ernest emphasizes full-service capability — combining design, manufacturing, and distribution under one roof — along with a sustainability focus that aligns with Idaho initiatives. Its temperature-controlled packaging aims to maintain precise conditions for perishables and pharmaceuticals, while equipment automation targets reduced manual labor and smoother operations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom packaging design", "Food packaging", "Beverage packaging", "Pharmaceutical packaging", "Medical packaging", "Cosmetics packaging", "Retail packaging", "Display packaging", "Branded packaging", "Sustainable packaging", "Temperature-controlled packaging", "Industrial packaging", "Packaging equipment integration", "Packaging supply management", "Facility supply management"], "industries": ["Food & Beverage", "Pharmaceutical", "Medical", "Healthcare", "Cosmetics", "Retail", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Plant-based plastics", "Moisture-resistant sustainable coatings", "Corrugated", "Poly bags"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service packaging solutions (design, manufacturing, distribution)", "Nationally operated with local presence across Idaho", "Sustainable, biodegradable, and recyclable packaging options", "Temperature-controlled packaging for cold-chain compliance", "Packaging equipment automation and line integration"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Nampa, Idaho -> db", "Boise facility serves Idaho and beyond -> /", "Design, manufacturing, distribution of food packaging -> db", "Custom packaging for food, beverage, pharmaceutical, medical, cosmetics, retail, display, industrial -> /", "Branded, sustainable, temperature-controlled, industrial packaging -> /", "Packaging equipment: conveyor systems, case sealers, line integration -> /", "Packaging supply with just-in-time inventory and bulk order management -> /", "Facility supply solutions -> /", "Client examples: The Rag Company, Sol-ti, Pizza Port Brewing, No Toil, Carolina Coops, Coast Aluminum, 7 Points -> /", "Leadership: Stephen Turgeon (Regional VP), Nathan Morton (Director of Client Relations) -> /", "Nationally operated with local touch -> /", "Sustainable packaging aligned with Idaho initiatives -> /", "Temperature-controlled packaging for cold chain -> /", "Plant-based plastics and moisture-resistant sustainable coatings -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "design, manufacturing and distribution of high-quality food packaging solutions", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ernest-packaging-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ESCO Manufacturing Inc. was founded in 1965 in Watertown, South Dakota, where it remains headquartered. The company operates two dedicated facilities in the state and has spent over half a century as a wholesale sign manufacturer serving the Midwest and beyond.

The company produces custom signs, channel letters, cabinets, and faces, offering full-service manufacturing from design assistance through final production. Its team of tenured professionals handles projects of any size, style, or quantity, including specialized church, school, and municipal signage. The operation emphasizes precision and the capacity to manage complex, large-scale projects.

