UPDATE companies SET description='The FARM Food Processing Accelerator is located in Muskegon, Michigan. It was developed by the West Michigan Food Processing Association (WMFPA) in conjunction with the Community Foundation for Muskegon County and Muskegon Community College. A State of Michigan infrastructure grant of over $2 million awarded in 2019 enabled the project to move from plan to reality. Construction began in June 2020 and the facility was completed in early 2021.

The accelerator provides 8,000 square feet of flexible, food-grade manufacturing space designed for commercial fruit and vegetable processing. The facility meets USDA and FDA requirements and features loading docks, refrigeration and freezer storage, energy-efficient systems, and waste and water handling. Tenants supply their own processing equipment and occupy individual suites with flexible lease terms. The site also hosts the Michigan State University Mobile Processing Lab, which supports research, education, and workforce training.

FARM serves early-stage and growing food processing companies seeking a bridge from kitchen incubators to full commercialization. Target clients include entrepreneurial ventures at stage one or two, as well as established firms needing offsite test manufacturing. The center draws on partnerships with Michigan State University and Muskegon Community College to link students and researchers with industry projects.

The initiative was created to strengthen West Michigan''s food processing sector by providing a dedicated scale-up facility, attracting venture capital, and integrating academic resources with commercial production. WMFPA technical experts also noted the facility''s potential as essential infrastructure for emergency response, such as repackaging sanitizer during the COVID-19 pandemic.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food-grade industrial space leasing", "Flexible manufacturing for fruit and vegetable processing", "USDA/FDA compliant facility", "Loading dock access", "Refrigeration and freezer storage", "Waste and water handling", "MSU Mobile Processing Lab access", "Product development incubation", "Business development support", "Education and workforce training partnerships"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Fruit and vegetable processing", "Renewable energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Loading docks", "Refrigeration/freezers", "Waste and water handling systems", "MSU Mobile Processing Lab"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Food-grade industrial space with individual suites and flexible lease options", "8,000 sq ft flexible manufacturing space for commercial fruit and vegetable processing", "Facility complies with USDA and FDA requirements", "Located on Muskegon Community College campus with Michigan State University affiliation", "On-site MSU Mobile Processing Lab for research and training"], "facts_used": ["Location: Muskegon, Michigan -> pages:/", "Developed by WMFPA, Community Foundation for Muskegon County, Muskegon Community College -> pages:/", "State of Michigan infrastructure grant >$2M awarded in 2019 -> pages:/", "Construction began June 2020, completed early 2021 -> pages:/", "8,000 sq ft flexible manufacturing space for fruit/vegetable processing -> pages:/", "USDA/FDA compliant facility with loading docks, refrigeration, waste/water handling -> pages:/", "Tenants furnish own equipment, flexible lease terms -> pages:/", "Located on Muskegon Community College campus with MSU affiliation -> pages:/", "MSU Mobile Processing Lab on site -> pages:/", "Seeking tenants, contact Clarence Rudat -> pages:/", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "FARM (Food, Agriculture, Research, Manufacturing Center) accelerator and business development center targeted at stage one or two entrepreneurial companies or existing mature ones that are looking for an offsite location for test manufacturing of new products.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/81299091/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='farm-food-processing-accelerator' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='FCPS Electric is headquartered in Bryant, Arkansas, and was founded in 1977 by Lorin Fleming. What began as a one‑man electrical contracting operation has grown into an independently owned, multi‑state service company with a full team of factory‑trained technicians. The business remains based in Bryant and serves commercial and industrial facilities across Arkansas, Tennessee, Texas, Alabama, Iowa, Louisiana, and Mississippi.

The company provides full‑service electrical contracting, including design‑build, installation, and maintenance of power generation and distribution systems. Core capabilities cover medium‑ and high‑voltage switchgear, standby and prime‑power generators, custom power distribution panels, cable and wire installation, industrial automation and controls, network cabling and security integration, aerial lift services, and petroleum‑fuel‑system electrical work. A 24/7 emergency response team handles troubleshooting, equipment failure, and scheduled inspections.

Clients span healthcare, manufacturing, water treatment, and petroleum retail. Long‑term accounts include the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (controls and electrical projects), Ryerson (machine controls), and Conway County Regional Water (a 7 MGD treatment plant and 23 remote sites). The firm also serves convenience‑store fuel systems and general commercial and industrial facilities throughout its licensed territory.

Fleming started FCPS on the principle that electrical work should be done right the first time, with relationships valued over transactions. The company emphasizes that its independent ownership allows it to answer emergency calls at any hour, invest heavily in factory certifications, and maintain multi‑decade client partnerships without pressure from outside investors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical design & build", "Switchgear installation & service (medium/high voltage)", "Generator installation & maintenance", "Power distribution panel design, fabrication & installation", "Cable & wire installation", "Electrical troubleshooting & repair", "Preventive maintenance & inspections", "Industrial automation & controls", "Network cabling & security integration", "Aerial lift / bucket truck services", "Petroleum/fuel system electrical", "24/7 emergency electrical service", "Component sourcing & procurement", "Panel wiring & assembly"], "industries": ["Healthcare / hospitals", "Manufacturing", "Water / wastewater treatment", "Petroleum / convenience stores", "Commercial facilities", "Industrial facilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24/7 live emergency response \u2014 technicians answer the phone at 2\u202fAM", "Factory\u2011trained and certified technicians on every project", "Independently owned, local decision\u2011making with multi\u2011state licensing", "Decades\u2011long client relationships (20+ years with some accounts)", "Comprehensive design\u2011build through maintenance under one contract"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: 212 McClanahan Drive, Bryant, AR 72022 -> /", "Founded 1977 by Lorin Fleming -> /about-us", "Independently owned, still based in Bryant -> /about-us", "Licensed in AR, TN, TX, AL, IA, LA, MS -> /", "Services: design-build, switchgear, generators, panels, automation, network/security, aerial lift, petroleum electrical, 24/7 emergenc