UPDATE companies SET description='Fabricated Steel Products (FSP) operates two fabrication shops in Baton Rouge, Louisiana. The company was founded in 1986 by Warren Tabor and remains family‑owned, serving the Gulf Coast region and beyond with structural and miscellaneous steel fabrication.

FSP provides structural steel fabrication, steel detailing, and engineered connection design, along with custom services such as galvanizing, plate forming, structural coating, sandblasting, and painting. The facility averages 600–900 tons of output per month and employs 75 people, including master fabricators and engineers. Equipment includes a fully automated Voortman beam line with layout, CNC plasma tables, drill lines, punch lines, and forming equipment. The shop also uses barcode tracking for every piece and offers in‑house detailing and connection design via SDS/2 and Tekla for BIM coordination and clash detection.

The fabricator supplies steel to the oil, gas, petrochemical, power, paper and pulp, food processing, automotive, municipal, and defense industries. Customers range from large industrial projects to smaller orders across the Gulf Coast and internationally.

FSP emphasizes its AISC certification as a Structural Steel Building Fabricator, a family‑owned culture focused on continuous improvement, and a commitment to on‑time delivery. The company highlights barcode traceability, integrated BIM detailing, and a combined staff experience of over 150 years as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['AISC Certified Fabricator (Structural Steel Building Fabricator)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Miscellaneous steel fabrication", "Steel detailing", "Engineered connection design", "Custom fabrication", "Galvanizing", "Plate forming", "Structural coating", "Sandblasting", "Painting", "Barcode tracking", "BIM project services", "Clash detection"], "industries": ["Oil and gas", "Petrochemical", "Power generation", "Paper and pulp", "Food processing", "Automotive", "Municipal", "Defense"], "materials": ["Structural steel"], "equipment": ["Voortman beam line with layout", "CNC plasma tables", "CNC drill lines", "CNC punch lines", "Layout equipment", "Forming equipment", "SDS/2 software", "Tekla software"], "volume": "600-900 tons per month", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AISC certified Structural Steel Building Fabricator", "Two fabrication shops in Baton Rouge", "Monthly capacity of 600\u2013900 tons", "Barcode tracking of every fabricated piece", "In\u2011house detailing and connection design with SDS/2 and Tekla"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 by Warren Tabor -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "75 employees -> /about-us", "Two shops in Baton Rouge -> /", "AISC certified fabricator -> /", "Volume 600-900 tons per month -> /", "Voortman beam line -> /", "CNC plasma tables, drill lines, punch lines, layout, forming equipment -> /", "Barcode tracking -> /", "SDS/2 and Tekla for BIM -> /", "Industries served: oil, gas, petrochemical, power, paper & pulp, food processing, automotive, municipal, defense -> /", "Galvanizing, plate-forming, structural coating, sandblast