UPDATE companies SET description='Falcon Engineering Corporation operates from Mesa, Arizona, as a women-owned small business specializing in mission-critical tactical textiles and parachutes. The company has been in business for 12 years, building a reputation for engineering, cut-and-sew production, and inspection of safety-critical soft goods under a single AS9100 Rev D quality system.

The manufacturer produces whole-airframe recovery parachutes for Cirrus SR20, SR22, and SF50 Vision Jet aircraft, along with T-11 and MC-6 personnel parachutes for airborne operations, LCLV, G-12, and 26-foot cargo parachutes for aerial resupply, and decelerator parachutes for high-performance aircraft such as the B-52. Its capabilities span 3D and 2D modeling, first-article prototyping, skilled cut-and-sew of canopies, lines, and harnesses, and recurring production lots—evidenced by more than 10,000 parachutes shipped and 38 National Stock Numbers across Federal Supply Class 1670.

Customers include commercial aviation original equipment manufacturers and military procurement agencies across airborne, cargo, and deceleration mission areas, as well as the U.S. Forestry Service under specification 5100-86. The company also supplies tactical gear, slings, tie-downs, strap assemblies, and inflatables.

Falcon emphasizes that every product is treated as safety-critical, with engineering, manufacturing, and quality control consolidated under one roof to ensure soft goods work the first time. The women-owned designation and AS9100 Rev D certification underscore its focus on disciplined processes for prototype-to-production runs.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100 Rev D','ISO 9001:2015','Women-Owned Small Business']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering & prototyping (3D/2D modeling, first articles)", "Cut-and-sew production (canopies, lines, harnesses)", "Quality inspection & control", "Recurring production lots", "Parachute manufacturing (recovery, personnel, cargo, deceleration)", "Tactical gear manufacturing", "Slings manufacturing", "Strap assemblies", "Inflatables manufacturing", "CNC machining", "Fabrication", "Forestry Service (5100-86)"], "industries": ["Commercial aviation", "Military", "Forestry Service"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to production quantities; 10,000+ parachutes shipped", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineering, cut-and-sew, and inspection under one AS9100 Rev D quality system", "38 parachute NSNs across FSC 1670", "10,000+ parachutes shipped with 99% on-time delivery", "Women-Owned Small Business", "Prototype-to-production capability for safety-critical soft goods"], "facts_used": ["Mesa, Arizona headquarters -> /", "Women-Owned Small Business -> /", "AS9100 Rev D and ISO 9001:2015 certifications -> /", "12 years in business -> /", "10,000+ parachutes shipped -> /", "99% on-time delivery -> /", "38 parachute NSNs, FSC 1670 -> /", "Products: Cirrus SR20/SR22/SF50 recovery parachutes, T-11/MC-6 personnel parachutes, LCLV/G-12/26ft cargo parachutes, B-52 deceleration parachutes -> /", "Capabilities: engineering, prototyping, cut-and-sew, inspection, production volumes -> /", "Forestry Service (5100-86) -> db", "CNC / fabrication capabilities -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_