UPDATE companies SET description='Feast Detroit operates from Inkster, Michigan. The company was founded by a group of small food entrepreneurs with guidance from Eastern Market, which recognized a need for a facility to help small brands scale production. Cofounders Amit Makhecha (Managing Director) and Scott Owens lead the team.

The 16,000-square-foot climate-controlled facility provides contract manufacturing and private-label services for specialty foods. Capabilities include shelf-stable hot fill (acidified and acid), ambient fill (dry and liquid pack), cold fill with modified atmosphere packaging, a shared-use kitchen, and e-commerce fulfillment. The operation supports over 40 client companies and more than 100 SKUs.

Feast Detroit serves small and medium food brands, producing items such as salsas, chutneys, hot sauces, BBQ sauces, salad dressings, pickles, mustards, popped snacks, spice blends, pasta sauces, soups, and ready-to-eat entrées. Customers are typically local food entrepreneurs looking to expand beyond incubator kitchens.

The company was created to bridge the gap between shared-use kitchens and traditional co-packers that impose high minimum orders. Feast Detroit differentiates itself with low minimum order quantities, an average lead time of about three weeks, third-party GMP certification, and licensing from the Michigan Department of Agriculture and Rural Development (MDARD) plus FDA registration for acidified food production.', certifications=ARRAY['GMP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract manufacturing", "Private label production", "Shelf-stable hot fill (acidified)", "Shelf-stable hot fill (acid)", "Ambient dry pack", "Ambient liquid pack", "Cold fill modified atmosphere packaging", "Shared-use kitchen rental", "E-commerce fulfillment (order monitoring, packaging, shipping)", "Test kitchen access"], "industries": ["Specialty food products", "Small and medium food brands", "Local food brands"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "About 3 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Low minimum order quantities compared to traditional co-packers", "Average lead time of about three weeks", "Third-party GMP certification", "Licensed by MDARD and FDA registered for acidified food production", "16,000 sq ft climate-controlled facility with shared-use kitchen and e-commerce fulfillment"], "facts_used": ["Location: Inkster, Michigan -> db", "Founded by small food entrepreneurs with guidance from Eastern Market -> /about-us", "Cofounders: Amit Makhecha (Managing Director) and Scott Owens -> /about-us", "Facility: 16,000 sq ft climate-controlled production and warehousing space -> /services", "Supports over 40 companies and 100+ SKUs -> /about-us", "Capabilities: shelf-stable hot fill (acidified, acid), ambient fill (dry pack, liquid pack), cold fill (modified atmosphere packaging), shared-use kitchen, e-commerce fulfillment -> /services", "Products: salsas, chutneys, hot sauces, BBQ sauces, salad dressings, pickles, mustards, popped snacks, spice blends, pasta sauces, soups, ready-to-eat entr\u00e9es -> /services", "Low minimum order quantities -> /", "Average lead time about 3 weeks -> /", "Third-party GMP certification -> /", "Licensed by MDARD and FDA registered for acidified food production -> /services", "Company type: contract manufacturer / co-packing -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract manufacturer for Specialty food products supporting small and medium sized food brands", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='feast-detroit' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ferric, Inc. was founded in 2021 and is headquartered in New York, New York.

The company designs and manufactures integrated voltage regulators that combine controller, FETs, inductor, and capacitors into a single package. Its proprietary thin-film magnetic materials technology and CMOS-integrated ferromagnetic power inductor enable converters that are more than 10 times smaller than conventional discrete solutions. Ferric holds over 40 patents built on a decade of research and offers product lines including the Fe1728 flexible multi-output converter, the Fe1736 16-phase buck converter, the Fe1766 ultra-high current density IVR, and the Fe1767 Newport dual-sided IVR for vertical power delivery.

Ferric serves AI and data center operators, high-performance computing customers, and mobile and consumer electronics manufacturers. Its IVRs have been proven in Apple products since 2021 and are targeted at hyperscaler environments where energy reduction is critical. The company''s solutions scale across multiple power domains, supporting applications from AI accelerators to compact consumer devices.

Ferric states that its technology sets a new standard for current density, performance, and flexibility. The company emphasizes the highest current density in the industry (4.5 A/mm²), elimination of bulky discrete components with up to 74% component count reduction, and true vertical power delivery through dual-sided packaging. An ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system underpins its commitment to continuous improvement and customer satisfaction.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Integrated Voltage Regulator (IVR) design", "CMOS-integrated ferromagnetic power inductor technology", "Thin-film magnetic materials technology", "Vertical power delivery", "Back Side PCB Attach", "Land Side Package Attach", "Land Side with Dual-side Attach", "Substrate Embedded integration", "Die Side Package Attach", "PCB Embedded integration", "Multi-phase buck converter design", "Multi-output configurable power domains"], "industries": ["AI and Data Centers", "High-Performance Computing", "Mobile and Consumer Electronics", "Hyperscalers"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World''s smallest, most efficient IVRs", "Highest current density in industry (4.5 A/mm\u00b2)", "Eliminates bulky discrete components, reducing count up to 74%", "Proprietary thin-film magnetic materials technology", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2021 -> db", "Headquarters New York, NY -> db and homepage", "Semiconductor company pioneering IVRs -> homepage", "Proprietary thin-film magnetic materials technology -> homepage", "CMOS-integrated ferromagnetic power inductor technology -> homepage", "40+ patents, decade of research -> homepage", "Product lines: Fe1728, Fe1736, Fe1766, Fe1767 Newport -> homepage", "Current density 4.5 A/mm\u00b2, >10x smaller than conventional -> homepage", "Industries: AI and Data Centers, High-Performance Computing, Mobile and Consumer Electronics -> homepage", "Proven in Apple products since 2021 -> homepage products list", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> quality page", "RoHS compliance -> quality page", "Integration methods: Back Side PCB Attach, Land Side Package Attach, etc. -> homepage", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We build the world''s smallest, most efficient Integrated Voltage Regulators (IVRs).", "founded_year": "2021", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/ferric/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ferric-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Fiorenza Custom Woodworking operates from Lewisville, Texas, where third-generation master wood craftsman Wayne Fiorenza continues a family tradition that began in Italy. His grandfather learned the trade as a boy in Italy, passed it to his father, who then taught Wayne the craft. The company carries forward that lineage, emphasizing furniture built to last more than a lifetime.

The shop produces custom furniture, millwork, and architectural woodwork including wall units, entertainment centers, hidden doors, fireplace mantels, kitchen cabinets, home office systems, island countertops, home theater cabinetry, and bathroom vanities. Projects range from single pieces to whole-room installations for libraries, studies, kitchens, dining rooms, bedrooms, baths, and executive offices. No facility size or headcount is disclosed.

Clients are primarily residential homeowners and commercial office clients across the Dallas–Fort Worth metroplex. Recent work includes a hidden door in Plano, a cherry dining table in Denton, kitchen cabinets in Argyle, a reception desk in Grapevine, and a master bath vanity in Flower Mound.

Fiorenza cites its third-generation heritage, old-world Italian craftsmanship, and a commitment to timely, efficient execution as differentiators. Free estimates are offered, and the firm stresses that every piece is made to endure for generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom woodworking", "Millwork", "Custom furniture", "Wall units", "Entertainment centers", "Hidden doors", "Fireplace mantels", "Kitchen cabinets", "Home office cabinetry", "Island wood countertops", "Home theater cabinetry", "Bathroom vanities"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial office"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Third-generation woodworking heritage", "Furniture built to last generations", "Old-world Italian craftsmanship", "Free estimates on custom projects", "Timely and efficient project execution"], "facts_used": ["Company name and location: Fiorenza Custom Woodworking, Lewisville, Texas -> db", "Founder: Wayne Fiorenza, third-generation master wood craftsman -> db (description) and homepage", "Family lineage: grandfather learned in Italy, passed to father, then to Wayne -> db (description)", "Services: custom furniture, millwork, wall units, entertainment centers, hidden doors, fireplace mantels, kitchen cabinets, home office, island countertops, home theater, bathroom vanities -> homepage", "Project examples in Irving, Plano, Aubrey, Argyle, Denton, Grapevine, Flower Mound, etc. -> homepage", "Serves residential and executive office spaces -> homepage", "Differentiators: third-generation heritage, old-world Italian craftsmanship, timely execution, free estimates -> homepage", "Contact: 171 S. Railroad St. #4 Lewisville, TX 75057 -> homepage", "No founding year, employee count, certifications, equipment, materials, volume, lead time, tolerances stated -> db/homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Wayne Fiorenza is a 3rd generation master wood craftsman, and he prides himself in making only high quality furniture to last for more than a lifetime.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='fiorenza-custom-woodworking' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Five Rivers Fabrication operates from Easton, Pennsylvania, where it was founded in 2020 by a father-and-son team.

The company provides structural steel fabrication, commercial signage, railings, custom fabrication, and home decor items. Its shop handles projects ranging from large-scale structural components to decorative wall art such as the Spartan Helmet Flag, and it also runs an online store for branded merchandise and smaller metal goods.

Clients span commercial construction firms needing structural steel and signage, architectural projects requiring railings, and residential customers seeking custom home decor. A noted reference is the veterans’ nonprofit Battle Borne, which has sourced signs and logo pieces for its organization and partners.

