UPDATE companies SET description='Florida Natural Flavors operates from a 32,000-square-foot facility in Casselberry, Florida. The company was founded in 1982 by Dave Erdman, who remains president, and is family-owned. Erdman''s goal was to bring high-quality beverage mixes to market that are easy to use, easy to store, and deliver strong profit margins for distributors.

The company manufactures fruit and juice-based beverage mixes, soda syrups, frozen drinks, daiquiri mixes, smoothies, juice concentrates, and bag-in-box products. Its Casselberry plant runs batches of 1,000 to 3,000 gallons and includes an in-house laboratory for quality control and an on-site printing facility for labels.

Customers include beverage distributors, restaurants, bars, hotels, resorts, theme parks, hospitality groups, convenience stores, cafés, cruise lines, and all-inclusive resorts. The company''s products are served worldwide through these channels.

Florida Natural Flavors differentiates itself by specializing solely in beverages, a focus the company says keeps it ahead in innovation and cost efficiency. It emphasizes family-oriented service, treating employees and distributors like family, and guarantees fast turnaround on stock and custom orders with rush-order accommodation. The facility is GSFI-certified, holds a Florida citrus dealer license, and undergoes regular FDA, USDA, and state agriculture inspections.', certifications=ARRAY['Global Safety Food Industry (GSFI) Certified','National Registry of Food Safety Professionals (NRFSP) Certified','Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) Trained and Certified','Kosher Certified (Florida-K)','State of Florida licensed citrus dealer']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Beverage manufacturing", "Contract packaging (co-packing)", "Private label beverage manufacturing", "Product development", "Flavor matching", "Bag-in-box packaging", "Bottling", "Labeling (in-house printing)", "Quality control (in-house laboratory)", "Frozen drink production", "Daiquiri mix production", "Soda syrup production", "Smoothie production", "Juice concentrate production", "Beverage contract manufacturing", "Turn-key packaging", "NDA signing for proprietary formulas", "Packaging: 1/2 gallon, gallon, bag-in-box 2.5/3/5 gallon"], "industries": ["Beverage distribution", "Restaurants & bars", "Hotels & resorts", "Theme parks & hospitality groups", "Convenience stores", "Cruise lines", "All-inclusive resorts", "Caf\u00e9s", "Food service"], "materials": ["Fruit and juice-based ingredients", "Soda syrup bases", "Fresh ingredients", "Citrus"], "equipment": [], "volume": "1,000 to 3,000 gallons per batch", "lead_time": "Fast turnaround on stock and custom products; rush orders accommodated", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Specializes solely in beverage manufacturing", "In-house label printing for faster turnaround", "State of Florida licensed citrus dealer", "GSFI-certified production facility", "Fast turnaround on stock and custom products with rush-order accommodation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 by Dave Erdman -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "Facility 32,000 sq ft in Casselberry, FL -> /services", "Batch capacity 1,000-3,000 gallons -> /services", "In-house laboratory and on-site printing -> /services", "Products: fruit/juice mixes, soda syrups, frozen drinks, daiquiri mixes, smoothies, juice concentrates, bag-in-box -> /, /services", "Services: contract packaging, private label, product development -> /services", "Industries served: distributors, restaurants, bars, hotels, resorts, theme parks, convenience stores, caf\u00e9s, cruise lines, all-inclusive resorts -> /, /about-us", "Certifications: GSFI, NRFSP, OSHA, HACCP, Kosher (Florida-K) -> /about-us", "Florida citrus dealer license, FDA/USDA/FL Dept of Ag inspections -> /about-us", "Fast turnaround, rush orders -> /", "Leadership: Dave Erdman (Founder/President), Garry L. Erdman (VP Ops), Jeffrey A. Smail (GM) -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Florida Natural Flavors is the premier manufacturer of the highest quality fruit and juice-based beverage mixes and soda syrups.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='florida-natural-flavors' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Foliot Furniture, headquartered in Las Vegas, Nevada, was founded in 1991 by Daniel Foliot, a former aspiring lawyer who left a woodworking venture to start his own company. The business began with a focus on furniture for daycares and primary schools before expanding into higher education and hospitality.

With a workforce of more than 630 employees, Foliot produces laminate casegoods, seating, and upholstery for high-use environments, delivering over 1.25 million rooms to date. In 2024, it deployed 17 collaborative robots across its production lines.

Foliot serves student housing, hospitality, community living, staff housing, government, and maritime sectors. Clients include Savannah College of Art and Design, Cornell University, La Maison des Parents d''Enfants Handicapés des Laurentides, Spacesaver Interiors, and Ovation. The firm emphasizes vertical integration to control quality and lead times, with manufacturing in both the United States and Canada.

Foliot differentiates itself through vertically integrated manufacturing, warranties, and lifecycle support programs. The company cites its in-house design-to-delivery process, binational footprint, and commitment to safety—recordable injuries have fallen nearly 80% since 2019—as key advantages. A 2020 investment from Novacap supports continued expansion.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial furniture design and engineering", "Laminate casegoods manufacturing", "Seating and upholstery production", "In-house project management and logistics", "Design advisory and personalization", "Quick-ship program for select products", "Cobot-assisted assembly and fabrication"], "industries": ["Student Housing", "Hospitality", "Community Living", "Staff Housing", "Government", "Maritime", "Educational Housing"], "materials": ["Laminate", "Upholstery fabrics"], "equipment": ["Collaborative robots (Cobots) \u2013 17 units deployed 2024"], "volume": "Over 1.25 million rooms delivered", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated design, engineering, and manufacturing in-house", "Over 1.25 million rooms delivered across North America", "Three manufacturing facilities in the U.S. and Canada", "17 collaborative robots deployed in production (2024)", "Industry-specific warranties and lifecycle replacement programs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1991 by Daniel Foliot -> /about-us", "Headquarters Las Vegas, Nevada -> db", "3 North American manufacturing facilities -> /", "630+ employees -> db", "Over 1.25 million rooms delivered -> /", "Vertically integrated manufacturing -> /", "Industries: student housing, hospitality, community living, staff housing, government, maritime -> /, /about-us", "17 Cobots deployed 2024 -> /about-us", "Novacap investment 2020 -> /about-us", "Laminate furniture and seating/upholstery -> /about-us", "Client examples: Savannah College of Art and Design, Cornell University, etc. -> /", "Industry-leading warranties & lifecycle support -> /", "Design, engineering, production in-house -> /", "Operations in Canada and United States -> /", "Recordable injuries reduced nearly 80% since 2019 -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Foliot is an industry-leading commercial furniture manufacturer specializing in engineered interior solutions for living spaces where performance, durability, and design matter.", "founded_year": "1991", "employee_count": "630+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='foliot-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Food Processing Equipment Company, LLC operates from Kalamazoo, Michigan.

The firm buys, sells, and rebuilds used equipment for fresh vegetable, fruit, refrigeration, ice, freezing, cannery, and packaging lines. Its inventory includes individual machines such as conveyors, peelers, shredders, optical sorters, and drying systems, as well as complete processing plants. In addition to equipment sales, the company provides brokerage, auction, and investment recovery services, along with appraisals, line layout, installation, equipment financing, leasing, and consultation. It also supplies new Urschel blades for mechanical cutting machines.

The customer base spans food processors worldwide, ranging from small operations needing a single machine to large facilities requiring entire production lines. The company serves sectors including fresh and frozen produce, canned goods, and packaged foods.

